d isinstance(c, int)):\n        raise TypeError("All arguments must be integers")\n    \n    if a == b == c:\n        return 3\n    elif a == b or a == c or b == c:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 0\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Reasoning\n\n- The function checks if all three arguments are integers using `isinstance()`.\n- It uses boolean expressions to compare the three values:\n  - `a == b == c` checks if all three are equal.\n  - `a == b or a == c or b == c` checks if exactly two values are equal.\n- The function returns 0 if all three are distinct.\n\nThis solution strictly adheres to the company\'s code quality standards and ensures static type checking via `mypy`.\n\n---\n\n### 📦 File Structure\n\n`experiments/solution.py` contains the implementation of the function. The directory structure is intact, and the file is placed in the correct location.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Output\n\nThe implementation is ready for use and follows all the rules and best practices required.'
