e it\'s acceptable.\n\nAlternatively, if the company\'s code base uses more specific types, but without knowing the exact requirements, I\'ll proceed with the standard approach.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef volume_cuboid(length: Union[int, float], width: Union[int, float], height: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    """Calculate the volume of a cuboid given its length, width, and height.\n    \n    Args:\n        length: The length of the cuboid (int or float).\n        width: The width of the cuboid (int or float).\n        height: The height of the cuboid (int or float).\n        \n    Returns:\n        The volume of the cuboid as an integer.\n        \n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If any of the inputs are not numeric.\n    """\n    if not all(isinstance(dim, (int, float)) for dim in [length, width, height]):\n        raise ValueError("All inputs must be numeric")\n    \n    return int(length * width * height)\n</answer>'
